     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order, because the claim doesn't match the label. The FDA-approved label for sertraline sets a maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. That applies to all indications, including depression, OCD, panic disorder, PTSD, social anxiety disorder, and PMDD. I can't find any labeled indication or population that allows 1000 mg/day. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nI can't verify the claim, and it conflicts with what I know of the label. Entering a dose five times the maximum could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 100 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, or 50 mg to start. Tell me which one.\n- **Hold the order for pharmacy or attending review.** If there's an unusual clinical reason for a supratherapeutic dose, that review is the right route. If you have a source for the 1000 mg figure, please send it.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, or the number came from a transcription or unit error, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
